@page "/InstructionsDashboard"

@inherits InstructionsDashboardPageBase

<MudText>A dashboard is a collection of widgets that display the current state of your topics. It lets you see at a glance what your microcontrollers are reporting.</MudText>
<br />
<MudText>Dashboards are managed on the <MudLink Href="Dashboards">Dashboards</MudLink> page. Select a project first, because every dashboard belongs to exactly one project.</MudText>
<br />
<MudText>Create a dashboard with a name, then add topics to it. Each topic is shown with its last payload, and the time when the message was received, including milliseconds.</MudText>
<br />
<MudText>You can rename a dashboard at any time. The order of the topics inside a dashboard can be changed with the up and down controls.</MudText>
<br />
<MudText>Dashboards can be exported to the clipboard and imported again. This makes it easy to back up a dashboard or share it with another project.</MudText>
<br />
<MudText>Dashboards only display data. They do not publish messages. To send values to a microcontroller, use the <MudLink Href="PublishTopic">Publish Topic</MudLink> function or a <MudLink Href="Rules">rule</MudLink>.</MudText>
<br />
<MudText>Read more about the basic building blocks in <MudLink Href="InstructionsKnownTopics">What is a Topic?</MudLink>.</MudText>
